/P 51 0 R
/E (In Ukraine, from the moment I arrived in Zaporizhzhia to the moment I returned to Poland, I was never at ease. That feeling came less from the prospect of a weaponized drone striking me than from knowing that being seen by a Russian drone could bring artillery fire. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (I am not convinced our counter-drone priorities fully reflect that distinction. An unarmed drone can complete its mission by passing a usable location to a firing unit. Shooting it down afterward may do little for the soldiers it has already exposed.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
94 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (That makes defeating drone-enabled intelligence, surveillance, and reconnaissance a broader task. It includes concealment, deception, disrupting observation and reporting, and training units to respond when they believe they have been detected. It also requires a shared picture of what is overhead, including friendly drones, and procedures that let people act on that information. I want us to measure success partly by whether a formation can keep operating without being effectively targeted.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
