/P 54 0 R
/E (My reference point is my experience as a forward observer. What makes that role useful is the system around it: training, standardized reporting, communications, and understood responsibilities linking observation to fires. Counter-UAS needs an equivalent connection between detection and action. The observing function may be distributed across people and machines, and the engagement rules will differ by setting. The useful takeaway is that those relationships must be established and rehearsed before a threat appears. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
